(276 "2026-09-27T08:50:21Z" "claude" add "T68" "Measure the graph on note 12's real projects and record the numbers")
(277 "2026-09-27T08:50:21Z" "claude" add "T69" "Language-aware docs for the graph: help, skill, README known limits")
(278 "2026-09-27T08:50:29Z" "claude" note "T55" "Demoted to an optional precision upgrade per the XL3 code-graph design (see notes/12 follow-up): cs-extract (T63) gives an exact-enough, no-SDK C# graph and API shape via the generic extract/resolve-import contract every language implements. T55 stays useful when a .NET 10 SDK IS present (raises declared-> exact confidence, real diagnostics), but nothing downstream requires it anymore - T56 no longer depends on it.")
(279 "2026-09-27T08:50:29Z" "claude" edit "T55" "--priority")
(280 "2026-09-27T08:50:43Z" "claude" edit "T56" "--add-after --goal --rm-after")
(281 "2026-09-27T08:50:43Z" "claude" note "T56" "Re-pointed from T55 to T67 (shape-lock): T67 already delivers a working, no-SDK C# API lock via the generic extract/resolve-import contract (cs-extract, T63), so this task no longer blocks on the Roslyn worker. It becomes an optional precision layer on top of the default path, not a required one - matches the same demotion applied to T55.")
(282 "2026-09-27T08:50:55Z" "claude" edit "T57" "--add-after --goal --rm-after --title")
(283 "2026-09-27T08:50:55Z" "claude" note "T57" "Re-scoped onto the XL3 code-graph design (T58-T69) rather than the original T54/T55/T56 chain, after the design review concluded T55 (Roslyn worker) and T56 (its C# baseline) should be optional precision upgrades, not required dependencies - the generic extract/resolve-import contract (implemented once per language: rkt-extract/py-extract/cs-extract) already gives every language a no-toolchain API lock via shape-lock (T67). T54 (Python ast-based lock) stays a real dependency of T67, so it isn't removed, just no longer wired to a bespoke lock format. See notes/12 cross-language review's XL3 follow-up design for the full reasoning.")
(284 "2026-09-27T08:51:18Z" "claude" edit "T54" "--goal")
(285 "2026-09-27T08:51:18Z" "claude" note "T54" "Reworded (no behavior change) so its output is explicitly framed as feeding shape-lock's (T67) generic entry-shape field rather than a Python-only lock format - part of the XL3 code-graph design's re-scoping of T54-T57.")
(286 "2026-09-27T08:51:35Z" "claude" add "T70" "XL3 · Code graph, entry points and reachability")
